WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
The physical dangers of medical research
are easy to spot, but vulnerability

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.440
can also be manufactured. Take Northern
Ireland during the decades of

3
00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.040
sectarian violence known as the Troubles.

4
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.620
Researchers at Boston College launched the
Belfast Project, an oral history

5
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:21.780
initiative aimed at collecting candid
testimonies directly from former

6
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:27.180
paramilitaries. To get combatants to talk
on tape, the researchers offered a

7
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:32.820
strict condition— absolute ironclad
guarantees of academic confidentiality.

8
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.920
The problem was the material itself.

9
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.660
The interviewers were actively soliciting
recorded confessions to unsolved

10
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.680
murders and bombings. The academic drive
to preserve historical truth created

11
00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:51.140
a massive blind spot. The researchers
failed to account for the legal exposure

12
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.220
they were handing to their participants.

13
00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.580
When law enforcement agencies caught wind
of the tapes, they issued subpoenas

14
00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.020
to seize the university's records for
criminal investigations.

15
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.520
This graphic highlights the resulting
collision, the academic promise of

16
00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.440
confidentiality clashing with the reality
of legal subpoenas.

17
00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.080
Looking down the slide, we see the
fallout.

18
00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.900
Participants who spoke freely, believing
the university would protect them,

19
00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.420
were thrust into immense legal and
political jeopardy.

20
00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.620
Ethicists call this study-induced
vulnerability.

21
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.980
The very design of the Belfast Project
actively manufactured a risk for these

22
00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.840
individuals that did not exist before they
sat down at the microphone.

23
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:35.380
Academic ambition holds zero weight
against a criminal justice mandate.

24
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:39.840
Institutional protections have hard
borders, and crossing them puts human

25
00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.320
subjects directly in the line of fire.
